                <pb facs="0393" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1941-43/pg319"/>

                <head>Annex “C”</head>
                <p>Draft telegram from British Chiefs of Staff to Chiefs of Staff Committee,
                    London:</p>
                <p>Please put following to Lord Privy Seal:</p>
                <p>It is of highest importance that General Wavell should exercise supreme command
                    without delay, as soon as he reports himself ready to do so.</p>
                <p>Please propose to Dutch and Australian Governments that as soon as General Wavell
                    reports himself as ready he should be authorized to assume command, pending the
                    acceptance by those Governments of the ABDA machinery as set out in Annex II of
                    his directive.</p>
                <p>United States Chiefs of Staff agree.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
